# DOI: assigned by Zenodo after a published GitHub release is archived.
# Do not add a doi or identifiers entry until that DOI exists.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
  Cite this repository only as a small geometric mask baker.
  For continuous flash suppression, cite Tsuchiya and Koch (2005).
  For controlled Mondrian / CFS mask construction and analysis, cite
  Wang, Alais, Blake, and Han (2022; CFS-crafter).
type: software
title: "MaskingGenerator: geometric Mondrian-like mask frames for CFS/RMS-style work"
abstract: >-
  Browser page that bakes geometric Mondrian-like mask frames
  (random rectangles, circles, or triangles on a gray canvas) and
  downloads them as a ZIP of PNGs. Intended as a lightweight baker
  for CFS / RMS-style work, not as a stimulus-analysis or
  experiment-presentation tool.
authors:
